# Cafe Sales Data Analysis & Business Intelligence

## Project Overview
This project presents an end-to-end Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) based on a cafe's daily transaction records. The primary objective is to transform raw, inconsistent sales data into actionable business intelligence. The analysis provides data-driven recommendations to help management optimize inventory, improve staff scheduling, and maximize overall revenue.

## Technical Stack
* Language: Python
* Data Manipulation & Engineering: Pandas, NumPy
* Data Visualization: Matplotlib, Seaborn
* Environment: Jupyter Notebook

## Data Engineering & Memory Optimization
Before conducting the analysis, rigorous data cleaning and preprocessing pipelines were implemented to ensure data integrity and computational efficiency:
* Anomaly Detection & Handling: Identified and parsed dirty text strings (e.g., hidden ERROR values) within temporal data, safely coercing them into valid datetime objects.
* Missing Value Imputation: Strategically handled missing categorical data across location and payment columns without arbitrarily dropping rows, preserving the statistical significance of the dataset.
* Memory Footprint Reduction: Optimized data structures by converting low-cardinality text columns (Item, Payment Method, Location) from standard object types to pandas category types, significantly reducing the dataset's memory usage and improving computational speed.

## Key Business Insights & Recommendations

### 1. Volume vs. Revenue Dynamics
* Observation: Coffee drives the highest transaction volume (foot traffic), whereas food items like Salads generate the highest total overall revenue. 
* Business Impact: Recommends utilizing high-volume beverages as traffic drivers while training point-of-sale staff to actively cross-sell high-margin food items.

### 2. Operational Logistics (In-Store vs. Takeaway)
* Observation: Customer behavior is heavily item-dependent. Beverages and baked goods lean toward Takeaway, while full meal items are preferred In-Store.
* Business Impact: Informs store layout optimization—suggesting the relocation of the beverage pick-up counter closer to the exit to expedite Takeaway orders, while reserving dining space for higher-revenue In-Store customers.

### 3. Average Order Value (AOV) Analysis
* Observation: The Average Order Value remains statistically identical across all payment methods (Cash, Credit Card, Digital Wallets). 
* Business Impact: Advises management to avoid investing in costly promotions aimed at shifting payment behaviors, focusing instead on overarching upsell strategies.

### 4. Time-Series & Staffing Trends
* Observation: Analyzed customer traffic patterns by day of the week and tracked average daily revenue across generalized monthly cycles.
* Business Impact: Provides a quantitative foundation for labor management, allowing the business to align its highest-performing staff and inventory prep with empirically proven peak hours and days.

## How to Run the Project
1. Clone this repository to your local machine.
2. Install the required dependencies using pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn
3. Launch the environment via Jupyter Notebook.
4. Open the EDA-Practice.ipynb file and execute the cells sequentially to view the data pipeline and visualizations.
